Edge-lens review complete. 12 verified findings written to `lenses/edge-b.json` — every one traced mechanically from the changed lines and confirmed against the worktree source:

**Blockers (6)**
1. All four `client.gleam` demo call sites discard the mutated store (`let _ = next` at 2537/5959/6161/6275) — demo create lands on an error page, edits silently no-op, auto-open reverts.
2. `demo_api.download` uses `request.from_uri` on a relative URI — gleam_http requires a host, so the mock report download always fails.
3. `string.drop_start(analysis_id, 3)` maps `"an-aoife"` → `"aoife"`, but the baked PDFs/filename table are keyed `"a-aoife"` — would 404 even with a valid request.
4. `refetch_refcheck_effect` has no demo branch — every demo refcheck action fires a real unauthenticated API GET and breaks the detail page.
5. `UserClickedMarkAllRejected`/`UserClickedMarkSelectedRejected` aren't intercepted by `demo_update` — a real write POST to the live API from demo mode; `demo_api.bulk_reject_applications` is dead code.
6. `ApiReturnedRestoreVacancy` refetches via real `vacancy_api.fetch_archived` — demo restore 401s into a Failure page.

**Warnings (3):** bell toggle fires real fetch in demo; approval leaderboard read from pre-mutation store (permanently stale, no demo polling); reset on a sub-page leaves a permanent spinner (NotAsked, no refetch, no route change).

**Notes (3):** refcheck toast copy mismatch (snake_case vs kebab-case action names → "substituted" toast); notification dropdown never closes on click in demo; deterministic `id_suffix` collides for same-name demo vacancies.

Notably, the CI no-network lint (test.yml:130) greps only `client/src/demo/` — none of the four network leaks (which route through `client.gleam` arms) are caught by it.
